I work in a **Joint Replacement** unit: in hospital, hip and knee replacement is part of my daily practice. The shoulder remains my centre, but if you have a hip or knee problem I can assess it and, if needed, operate.

# Hip

Hip arthritis and total replacement, including minimally invasive approaches. Proximal femur fractures in the elderly, where replacement allows getting up quickly.

# Knee

Knee arthritis and total or unicompartmental replacement (when only one part of the knee is worn). I trained specifically on the Oxford partial knee.

# How to access

In the **public hospital** (Fucecchio) the pathway is the NHS one: GP referral and booking through the regional centre. **Privately**, you can book a visit through my office at the locations where I see patients.

# Honesty

If your hip or knee problem is complex and needs a super-specialist of that area, I will say so and refer you. I would rather tell you first than have you find out later.
